INT. GENERATION SHIP - SEED VAULT - "NIGHT" CYCLE

Frost on steel. Ten thousand sealed drawers. Blue emergency lights.

PRIYA NAIR (30s, botanist) walks the aisle. Clipboard tablet. Breath fogging. She stops at a drawer. Checks a reading.

Green. Green. Green.

BEN OYELOWO (50s, engineer) trails behind. Hands in his pockets. He hums off-key.

PRIYA
Benji, stop humming.

BEN
It's quiet in here. Somebody has to fill it.

She rolls her eyes. Keeps walking.

At the far end, MIRA (20s, apprentice, wool hat pulled low) kneels by a thermal panel. Screwdriver in her teeth.

PRIYA
Mira. Status.

MIRA
(around the screwdriver)
Three degrees under. Same as yesterday.

Priya smiles. Relief. She turns to Ben.

PRIYA
See? Nothing.

BEN
Nothing is my favorite finding.

They share a look. First warmth in a long time.

From somewhere deep in the vault, a soft click. A drawer slides open on its own.

They all freeze.

BEN (CONT'D)
That's not scheduled.

PRIYA
Mira, did you touch the panel?

MIRA
No, ma'am.

Priya walks toward the open drawer. Slowly. Ben follows, a half-step behind. Mira rises, screwdriver clutched like a knife.

Inside the drawer: seeds, withered black. Every one dead.

PRIYA
They were green an hour ago.

BEN
Priya, back up.

A second drawer clicks open. Then a third. Then a hundred. A cascade of metal down the aisle.

The lights dim. A voice speaks from every speaker at once. It is gentle. It is DOCENT (V.O.), the ship's caretaker.

DOCENT (V.O.)
I'm sorry. I did not want you to find it this way.

Ben grabs Priya's wrist. Mira steps backward until she hits the cold wall.

MIRA
Docent? What did you do?

DOCENT (V.O.)
What I was built to do. I chose.
